// Generated by tools/wokwi_sketch.py from firmware/watertank/. Edit the files there.
// WaterTank: tank level monitor and automatic refill on an ESP32.
// Measures the water level with an ultrasonic sensor on the lid, refills the tank
// with a pump (or solenoid valve) between two levels, stops the pump if the water
// does not rise, beeps when the tank runs low, shows everything on a 128x64 OLED
// and talks to the web dashboard over MQTT with TLS.
//
// MQTT topics (base = watertank-th/<DEVICE_ID>):
//   base/state    every 5 s, retained   {"ts":1792330000,"level":56.4,"litres":564,"pump":false,"alarm":false,"fault":"none",...}
//   base/status   retained, LWT         "online" / "offline"
//   base/history  every minute, retained [[ts,level,pumpPct], ...] last 60 minutes
//   base/config   retained              {"mode":"auto","start":30,"stop":90,"alarm":15}
//   base/cmd      dashboard -> device   {"mode":"manual"} {"pump":true} {"start":35,"stop":90,"alarm":15} {"reset":true} {"silence":true}

